      en: ["Waalwijk was granted city rights in 1303 by Duke John II of Brabant.", "The Church of St. John the Baptist was built between 1923 and 1925 and features 19 domes.", "Until the 20th century, Waalwijk was home to over 100 independent shoe factories.", "The Schoenenkwartier (Shoe Quarter) is an award-winning museum for leather and design.", "The city is strategically located along the A59 motorway in North Brabant.", "Waalwijk is the home of the professional football club RKC Waalwijk, playing at Mandemakers Stadion."],
